WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.404
"You will be kind to visitors," Onatah’s grandmother said.

2
00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:09.134
"These two can join the festival after Busk."

3
00:00:09.135 --> 00:00:13.808
She gave Onatah some old animal skins.

4
00:00:13.809 --> 00:00:16.473
"Put these in the fire."

5
00:00:16.474 --> 00:00:21.956
The children walked over to the large fire.

6
00:00:21.957 --> 00:00:25.403
"What is Busk?" Vinnie asked.

7
00:00:25.404 --> 00:00:32.280
"During the Green Corn Festival, we clean our homes completely," said Onatah.

8
00:00:32.281 --> 00:00:35.687
"We burn everything we do not use."

9
00:00:35.688 --> 00:00:40.010
Onatah threw the skins into the fire.

10
00:00:40.011 --> 00:00:42.759
People were staring at them.

11
00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:46.090
"Who are they?" asked one man.

12
00:00:46.091 --> 00:00:50.422
"Vinnie and Mandy," shrugged Onatah.

13
00:00:50.423 --> 00:00:54.213
"Grandmother welcomed them."

14
00:00:54.214 --> 00:00:58.545
"Then you are guests of the Onondaga," said the man.

15
00:00:58.546 --> 00:01:02.008
"Onondaga?" asked Mandy.

16
00:01:02.009 --> 00:01:04.811
The girl nodded proudly:

17
00:01:04.812 --> 00:01:09.133
"We are Onondaga, the People of the Hills.

18
00:01:09.134 --> 00:01:11.439
But Magua is Mohawk."

19
00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.951
She pointed to the man.

20
00:01:13.952 --> 00:01:20.684
"Five Indian nations make up the Iroquois, the People of the Longhouse," said Magua.

21
00:01:20.685 --> 00:01:23.173
He held up one hand.

22
00:01:23.174 --> 00:01:26.274
He counted five fingers:

23
00:01:26.275 --> 00:01:32.082
"Oneida, Cayuga, Onondaga, Seneca, and Mohawk."

24
00:01:32.083 --> 00:01:35.681
"Five nations?" asked Vinnie.

25
00:01:35.682 --> 00:01:40.124
"Yes, five nations became one people—the Iroquois!"said

26
00:01:40.125 --> 00:01:44.807
Magua, closing his hand into a fist. "Vinnie,

27
00:01:44.808 --> 00:01:47.680
do you like to fish?" "I’ve

28
00:01:47.681 --> 00:01:50.887
never tried it," said Vinnie. "I’ll

29
00:01:50.888 --> 00:01:54.806
teach you how we fish," said Magua. "Is

30
00:01:54.807 --> 00:01:59.149
it safe to split up?" Mandy asked Vinnie. "It’ll

31
00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:02.018
be fine," said Vinnie. He

32
00:02:02.019 --> 00:02:04.361
followed Magua. "Come,"

33
00:02:04.362 --> 00:02:09.477
said Onatah, warming to her new friend. "I’ll

34
00:02:09.478 --> 00:02:11.101
show you around. Then

35
00:02:11.102 --> 00:02:13.501
we’ll go to my house." They

36
00:02:13.502 --> 00:02:16.961
walked past the longhouses. Mandy

37
00:02:16.962 --> 00:02:21.748
saw an animal sign above every door. "What

38
00:02:21.749 --> 00:02:25.615
do these signs mean?" she asked. "Iroquois

39
00:02:25.616 --> 00:02:29.327
people belong to different clans. Clans

40
00:02:29.328 --> 00:02:37.759
are like big families that grow from one woman born long ago," explained Onatah. "Every

41
00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:40.695
clan has its own longhouse.

42
00:02:40.696 --> 00:02:44.268
I belong to the Bear Clan."

43
00:02:44.269 --> 00:02:49.489
The girls arrived at Onatah’s longhouse and went inside.

44
00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:54.255
"Let’s make a corn husk doll," suggested Onatah.

45
00:02:54.256 --> 00:02:58.672
She gave Mandy some corn hanging from the ceiling.

46
00:02:58.673 --> 00:03:05.103
Mandy also saw floor mats made from corn husks.

47
00:03:05.104 --> 00:03:09.667
"Is corn your main crop?" Mandy asked.

48
00:03:09.668 --> 00:03:16.095
"It is one of three vegetables we call the Three Sisters," Onatah replied.

49
00:03:16.096 --> 00:03:22.748
"Beans, squash, and corn must grow together as sisters do."

50
00:03:22.749 --> 00:03:26.407
Mandy and Onatah husked the corn.

51
00:03:26.408 --> 00:03:31.887
"Let’s get some beaver skin for a doll dress," said Onatah.

52
00:03:31.888 --> 00:03:35.805
The girls ran out the door.

53
00:03:35.806 --> 00:03:39.812
Vinnie and Magua got into a canoe.

54
00:03:39.813 --> 00:03:44.200
They paddled out on a nearby stream.

55
00:03:44.201 --> 00:03:48.004
"This is for you," said Magua.

56
00:03:48.005 --> 00:03:55.160
He gave Vinnie a long spear that was in the canoe.

57
00:03:55.161 --> 00:03:57.858
"You catch fish with this?"

58
00:03:57.859 --> 00:04:01.601
asked Vinnie, looking at his spear.

59
00:04:01.602 --> 00:04:04.559
"Watch," smiled Magua.

60
00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:10.765
He carefully aimed his spear and quickly pierced a fish.

61
00:04:10.766 --> 00:04:13.581
"Wow!" yelled Vinnie.

62
00:04:13.582 --> 00:04:16.502
"Is this how everyone does it?"

63
00:04:16.503 --> 00:04:21.528
"Only when we fish alone or with a friend," said Magua.

64
00:04:21.529 --> 00:04:25.023
"Mostly, we use the fish traps we’ve built."

65
00:04:25.024 --> 00:04:28.204
"Fish traps?" asked Vinnie.

66
00:04:28.205 --> 00:04:33.176
"The stream guides the fish into the trap," said Magua,

67
00:04:33.177 --> 00:04:37.541
pointing to a large circular dam made out of sticks.

68
00:04:37.542 --> 00:04:40.493
"Then we use a net to catch them."

69
00:04:40.494 --> 00:04:45.098
"Why are you in the Onondaga village?" asked Vinnie.

70
00:04:45.099 --> 00:04:46.872
"I am only visiting.

71
00:04:46.873 --> 00:04:51.474
My people live toward the rising sun," said Magua.

72
00:04:51.475 --> 00:04:54.477
"We are the Keepers of the Eastern Door.

73
00:04:54.478 --> 00:04:58.347
Mohawks protect the Iroquois from the whites in the East."

74
00:04:58.348 --> 00:05:03.015
Raising his spear, Magua moved with great speed.

75
00:05:03.016 --> 00:05:12.450
Then he speared another big fish.

